  "slug": "discovery-database-1f96",
  "summary": "ECOD 2027 and MobiDB 2027 add programmatic access layers, while DaliScope mines DALI structural-alignment sets for biological insight.",
  "synthesis": "Across these items, the common thread is making protein structural and disorder annotation programmatically accessible rather than only browsable. ECOD 2027 rebuilds its domain classification, reporting 2.9M domains with Foldseek-based sequence, structure, and keyword search, a new API, and synchronization with Pfam v38.2. MobiDB 2027 adds a refined controlled vocabulary, a versioned REST API and MCP server, Nextflow workflows, and static datasets aimed at machine-actionable use. DaliScope addresses the downstream side: it is an interactive Python framework that analyzes complete DALI structural-alignment target sets using community detection and Pfam annotation. The DaliScope item is a preprint, whereas the other two are published resources. The items are heterogeneous in scope, but their shared emphasis is interoperable, computationally tractable access to structural knowledge.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-12"
}
